6. Integration Theorem and Future Work

Integration Theorem (Year 2).
Assume H1, A2, and condition (C) from Theorem 3.1. Let \pi_S be the switched affordance policy from Theorem 4.3, and suppose the Lean‑verified IMDP model checker confirms \Phi_{\text{colony}} for a given colony configuration. Then:

· X_t > 0 a.s. and for every \delta>0 there exists \varepsilon_\delta>0 such that \liminf_{t\to\infty}\mathbb{P}[X_t\ge\varepsilon_\delta] \ge 1-\delta.
· V^{\pi_S} \ge V^* - \epsilon with computable \epsilon.
· The concrete colony satisfies the belonging property (P1) with probability at least 1-\delta (up to the verified abstraction error).

This theorem unifies the four theoretical pillars, providing a complete formal guarantee for meaning safety in extraterrestrial colonies under the stated assumptions.

Future Work.
Implementation and empirical validation of the Cultural Digital Twin (state estimation, model‑predictive control, real‑time verification monitor) are left for post‑doctoral or collaborative engineering efforts. The current dissertation provides the necessary mathematical protocols and proofs, ensuring that any future realisation rests on a rigorous foundation.

